name c01m07-corrosion
timeout 1800
time 1994-10-07T06:00:00Z

# ARMORED FIST (NovaLogic 1994), CAMPAIGN ONE "OVERWATCH", MISSION 7 OF 7 — `INDIA7`, CORROSION.
# THE SEVEN DISCLOSURES D1-D7 are stated in full in c01m01-slaughterzone.fbm and apply here unchanged.
#
# THE TASK [FSW]: sanction all COMMUNICATIONS LINKS, THEN all elements within the ENEMY COMPOUND.
# Course 136 SSE for Echo 1, ECHO 2 ON 186. Time limit 30 MIN — twice every other mission in the
# campaign and the only file in Overwatch with that limit [FSG].
#
# THE ORDER IS PART OF THE ORIGINAL'S VERDICT AND CANNOT BE JUDGED HERE. campaign.md §6 makes this the
# one mission where sequence decides: "the communications links AND THEN every element of the enemy
# compound". `objective` has no ordering in this format and `FBMissionMonitor` judges a set, not a
# sequence (doc/missions/verdict.md). The declaration below puts the comms links 2 km SHORT of the
# compound on Echo 1's own run-in, so the geometry enforces what the grammar cannot — a jet flying the
# axis reaches them first. That is a workaround in DATA, and it is not the same thing: nothing fails a
# run that takes them in the wrong order, because nothing can observe the order. NAMED, not hidden.
#
# THE HINDS ARE PRESENT AND HARMLESS. [GUIDE p.71] warns of "heavy Hind activity". Two `mi8` movers,
# for the reason and with the direction of error stated in c01m03-rubicon.fbm.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE DECLARES
#   Blue [GUIDE p.71]: Echo 1 = 3 M1A2 + 1 M3, Echo 2 = 1 M1A2 + 1 M3. SIX vehicles, six jets.
#   Red  [GUIDE p.71]: Bandit 1 (2 T-80, 2 BMP), Bandit 2 (3 T-80, 1 BMP — the BMP cell is marked `?`
#   in campaign.md and is declared as printed), Bandit 3 (3 T-80), Bandit 4 (1 T-80). Plus the comms
#   links and the compound.
#   Goals: the COMMS LINKS, the COMPOUND, and BANDIT 1 — the [FSW] task's second half is "all elements
#   WITHIN the enemy compound", and Bandit 1 is the platoon laid inside it at 1.5 km. WHICH platoon is
#   inside the compound is NOT stated by any source; Bandit 1 is taken by table order. Bandits 2-4 are
#   declared, attacked and are not goals. Neither the links nor the compound carries a count, so each
#   is declared ONCE (understated), and the goal flag is in the undecoded `DCBS` (campaign.md §7.4).
#
# THE 30-MINUTE LIMIT IS THE ONE MISSION-SHAPING NUMBER THAT SURVIVES THE SUBSTITUTION LEAST WELL. It
# was set for a company advancing on tracks through a mined approach; six jets at 231 m/s finish every
# pass inside 200 s and spend the remaining 1 600 s flying away. Kept because it is measured, and its
# emptiness is the substitution talking (D1).
#
# READING RULE (binding). The verdict is `m7e1a`'s UNIT_RESULT and nothing else.
#   SUCCESS/exit 0 requires the comms links, the compound and all four of Bandit 1 dead inside 1 800 s.
#   Two of Bandit 1 are T-80s, so the arithmetic says exit 3 (D4) and the interesting part is the rest:
#   the two soft installations should fall to one canister each, and Bandit 1's two BMPs to a third.
#   THE ORDER OF THE TWO INSTALLATION KILLS IS IN THE EVENT LOG and is the only place this campaign can
#   say anything about the original's sequence rule: report the two `damage CLUSTER` timestamps.
#   exit 1 on a blue unit is an ENGINE finding, not a mission loss (D2).

unit m7e1a
  module f16
  team friendly
  flight echo1 1
  spawn 25.25677 66.81289 960 136.0 450       # 40 km short of the compound on Echo 1's [FSW] course 136
  set gear up
  set fuel_int_pct 100
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 cbu87
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 25.01046 67.07453 960 450                # AIM POINT: the comms links, 2 km short of the compound
  wp 24.83546 67.26043 1560 450               # egress 25 km down Echo 1's axis
  objective kill unit m7comms
  objective kill unit m7cmpd
  objective kill unit m7b1v1
  objective kill unit m7b1v2
  objective kill unit m7b1v3
  objective kill unit m7b1v4
  objective survive

